            "created_at": "2025-09-23T11:33:42.08262+00:00",
            "notes": "#### Round 1\n\nTo build towards playing support, first we're gonna need to make money. Many build authors are tempted by [Siphon Gloves](item_099f8177-c2a4-4e13-b321-99349f8b1eb7) or [Ammo Reserves](item_982d53aa-5ef4-493f-93e7-9e374d0ebf34), but those are too expensive. You'l end up floating 500 which is inefficient. Instead, we'll bulk up with [Field Rations](item_46ae6709-1166-426f-bca3-97a538d3f089), [Electrolytes](item_274b7523-8273-4740-aa7b-837f3f143900), and [Ballistic Buffer](item_40146dd3-a8cb-40ca-8917-c430bfa2be0e).\n\n[Field Rations](item_46ae6709-1166-426f-bca3-97a538d3f089) is crazy because we can stay on point for a very long time and it heals a higher % of our health since we have such low base health. \n\n[Electrolytes](item_274b7523-8273-4740-aa7b-837f3f143900) is powerful for the same reason. We have low base health so flat increases are really good, plus both of these items' health increase is not affected by Tracer's stadium debuff. Plus you'll need electolytes come round 4 so it's better to buy it now.\n\n[Ballistic Buffer](item_40146dd3-a8cb-40ca-8917-c430bfa2be0e) for the same reason.\n\n[Refraction Armor](item_dd020802-8d00-489d-93e0-930b80e31144) would be excellent but there seems to be a bug and you cannot select it since tracer was hotfixed.",
