            "notes": "**Round 3**\n\nI know what you're thinking. \n\nYes.\n\nThat works.\n\nWhen you die with [Auto Recall](item_ae3dbebf-c306-4408-b698-6f666ace0a7c), you will stick your killer with [Pocket Bomb](item_83888c64-5648-4355-b546-674dde6b915c). Combined with [Bloodbound](item_d873e953-93cd-4b0d-8669-33184127cc3c), which APPLIES TO THE PERSON WHO TRIGGERS YOUR AUTO RECALL, this is going to NUKE. \n\n[Bloodbound](item_d873e953-93cd-4b0d-8669-33184127cc3c) is what's called a \"more multiplier\", meaning it adds the 10% at the end of the damage calculation. When you have a much of ability power, it is giving a much better relative percentage increase than 10% AP. It's more like 40% when you consider the in-built modifier from the [Pocket Bomb](item_4e5d5d1d-2c0d-4f5e-9521-9f71bdb88e9e) power.\n\n[Geneticist's Vial](item_c7443757-9e2a-4be8-b3a3-469ab64b0e9d) works with [Bloodbound](item_d873e953-93cd-4b0d-8669-33184127cc3c) and will set up for our round 5 combo",
